    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d332-a5">

                <pb facs="0451" n="377" sameAs="frus:frus1866p1/pg377"/>

                <head ana="#head_untitled-missing-head-in-printed-volume">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Headquarters District of the Rio
                                Grande</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">Brownsville,
                            Texas,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-12-23"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 23, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Major</hi>: I have the honor to enclose herewith, in
                    compliance with indorsement from headquaters military division of the gulf,
                    dated October 21, 1865, the proceedings of a board, appointed in obedience to
                    the above indorsement, to investigate the case of the alleged pillage of the
                    shipwrecked French merchant vessel Le Verrier, and the firing upon her crew by
                    soldiers of the United States, in February last, off Bagdad, Mexico,</p>
                <p>I am, sir, very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>G. WEITZEL, <hi rendition="#italic">Major General
                        Commanding.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Major <hi rendition="#small-caps">George Lee</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Assistant Adjutant General Military Division of the Gulf, New Orleans,
                            La.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
